1289-
1290-### Testing methodology
--
1292-A profile is ready for enforcement only when it passes all of the following test classes.
1293-
1294-| Test class | Purpose | Examples |
1295-|---|---|---|
1296:| Static compilation | Detect syntax, unsupported rules, missing includes, and deprecated constructs | `apparmor_parser -Q`, warning-as-error |
1297-| Structural lint | Detect obviously broad or dangerous policy | `ux`, `/** rw`, bare `capability,`, bare `network,`, `/dev/**`, writable code trees |
1298-| Positive functional | Confirm intended behavior | Startup, configuration load, normal data access, networking, rendering, CUDA execution |
1299-| Negative security | Confirm forbidden behavior fails | Read SSH keys, write `/etc`, execute shell, open unrelated devices, bind unexpected sockets |
1300:| Transition | Verify parent and child labels | Inspect `/proc/<pid>/attr/current` for browser, GPU, helper, and daemon processes |
1301-| Restart and reload | Verify policy replacement and process lifecycle | Reload profile, restart unconfined processes, check labels |
1302-| Failure path | Exercise errors, retries, crash reporting, cache rebuilds, and cleanup | Missing config, malformed input, disconnected network, disk-full simulation |
1303-| Compatibility | Verify Wayland, XWayland, portals, audio, GPU, CUDA, and user namespaces | GUI launch, file chooser, WebGL, VA-API, Vulkan, CUDA device query |
1304:| Performance | Detect policy-related regressions | Startup latency, process-spawn rate, browser tab launch, shader-cache behavior, CUDA launch |
1305:| Upgrade | Detect package and ABI drift | New executable paths, libraries, helper processes, device nodes, systemd directives |
