1515-### Migration plan for existing systems
1516-
1517-| Phase | Actions | Exit criterion |
1518-|---|---|---|
1519:| Baseline | Record Debian/kernel/AppArmor versions, loaded profiles, existing denials, services, launch paths, GPU devices, container workloads | Reproducible inventory and rollback snapshot |
1520:| Policy ownership | Assign profile owners and classify vendor, organization, and host-local policy | Every target has an accountable maintainer |
1521:| Low-risk scaffolding | Install abstractions, local hooks, wrappers, logging, and CI without enforcement | Policy compiles and no existing behavior changes |
1522:| Observe | Load selected profiles in complain mode and exercise structured workflows | Intended operations represented; unexplained events triaged |
1523-| High-value enforcement | Enforce network and privileged daemons first | Stable canaries with no unexplained denials |
1524:| Script migration | Replace direct interpreted-script launch paths with root-owned wrappers or units | All scheduled and interactive entrypoints verified |
1525-| Desktop migration | Enforce ordinary GUI apps before browsers and compositor | Wayland, portals, audio, and render acceleration pass |
1526-| Browser and GPU | Enforce browser and CUDA profiles with namespace/device tests | Internal sandbox, GPU, and negative tests pass |
1527:| Compositor and helpers | Profile privileged Wayland helpers and optionally Labwc | Explicit child transitions; no inherited desktop-wide profile |
1528-| Fleet rollout | Progressive host/user cohorts with automated rollback | Error and denial rates within agreed thresholds |
1529:| Continuous operation | Upgrade testing, policy reviews, drift detection, metrics | Policy lifecycle integrated into release engineering |
1530-
1531-Start with workloads where profile attachment is unambiguous and the consequence of denial is limited. Avoid beginning with PID 1 dependencies, SSH access, display login, Labwc, storage, or network-management components. Maintain an out-of-band administrative path during early enforcement.
