1692-
1693:A denial is not automatically an attack, and a lack of denials is not automatically success. Repeated library or cache denials may indicate compatibility drift; denied secret access may be a valuable security signal; and a process that never entered its profile generates no AppArmor denials at all. Runtime-label verification and functional metrics are therefore as important as audit-event collection.
1694-
1695:Permanent `flags=(audit)` or blanket audit rules can generate excessive logs on desktop and browser workloads. Prefer normal denial logging, targeted `audit` qualifiers for sensitive canaries, and time-bounded audit-all sessions during diagnostics. AppArmor’s policy language supports profile-wide audit mode and per-rule audit qualifiers. citeturn18search0
