    11	/usr/bin/perl rix,
    12	/usr/bin/perl5.[0-9]* rix,
    13	
    14	deny owner @{HOME}/perl5/ r,
    15	deny owner @{HOME}/perl5/** mrwkl,
    16	deny owner @{HOME}/.local/lib/perl5/ r,
    17	deny owner @{HOME}/.local/lib/perl5/** mrwkl,
    18	deny owner @{HOME}/.cpan/ r,
    19	deny owner @{HOME}/.cpan/** mrwkl,
    20	deny /root/ r,
    21	
    22	include if exists <local/managed-wrapper-perl>
--- Digital Assets README section ---
   200	
   201	Foot and the Kitty fallback render their font family and size from the selected
   202	desktop profile through `LABWC_TERMINAL_FONT_FAMILY` and
   203	`LABWC_TERMINAL_FONT_SIZE`; the managed profiles preserve the existing
   204	`Noto Sans Mono` size `12` baseline.
   205	
   206	Each new interactive Bash or Zsh instance in Foot or Kitty sources readable,
   207	non-symlinked `~/.profile.d/[0-9][0-9]-*.sh` fragments in lexical order. Login
   208	shells keep the fragments single-loaded, while non-login terminal shells still
   209	pick up managed addon environment such as development, firmware, and Vagrant
   210	paths. Nano uses the managed XDG configuration at
   211	`~/.config/nano/nanorc`, with line numbers, indentation and navigation
   212	defaults plus the standard, Debian-specific, and extra syntax-color bundles
   213	shipped by the installed `nano` package.
   214	
   215	Waybar keeps the existing `LABWC_WAYBAR_*` values as the external/default bar
   216	dimensions and adds `LABWC_WAYBAR_INTERNAL_*` overrides for the internal-output
   217	bar. The internal family covers bar height, taskbar/tray icons, font size, menu,
   218	workspace, taskbar and application buttons, compact status modules, quick
   219	controls, and lock/power button widths and padding.
   220	
   221	`Super+M` and `Ctrl+Alt+M` open the searchable **Computer Management**
   222	Fuzzel launcher.
   223	Its folder-style categories are Container Management, Remote Desktop,
   224	Endpoint Security, Digital Assets, Users & Groups, Network Management, System
   225	Configuration, Phone Management, Backup & Recovery, and Hardware &
   226	Peripherals. Firewall Security is nested below Endpoint Security instead of
   227	competing with it at the Computer Management root. The former
   228	`Ctrl+Super+A`, `Ctrl+Super+N`, `Ctrl+Super+P`, and `Ctrl+Super+R` bindings are
   229	retired so laptops and stationary systems share one management navigation
   230	model. Each category can override the shared Fuzzel menu sizing through
   231	`LABWC_FUZZEL_<CATEGORY>_WIDTH`, `LABWC_FUZZEL_<CATEGORY>_LINES`, and
   232	`LABWC_FUZZEL_<CATEGORY>_FONT_SIZE`, where `<CATEGORY>` is
   233	`CONTAINER_MANAGEMENT`, `REMOTE_DESKTOP`, `ENDPOINT_SECURITY`,
   234	`DIGITAL_ASSETS`, `USERS_GROUPS`, `NETWORK_MANAGEMENT`,
   235	`FIREWALL_SECURITY`, `SYSTEM_CONFIGURATION`, `PHONE_MANAGEMENT`,
   236	`BACKUP_RECOVERY`, or `HARDWARE_PERIPHERALS`.
   237	
   238	**Computer Management → Digital Assets** opens DOCX, PDF, and image action
   239	menus. Inputs are bounded regular files chosen only from `~/Downloads`,
   240	`~/Documents`, and `~/Desktop`; original files are never overwritten, and
   241	results are created with private permissions below
   242	`~/Documents/Digital-Assets`. The desktop package set provides Pandoc, QPDF,
   243	Poppler, ExifTool with ZIP support for DOCX metadata, GraphicsMagick, libvips,
   244	WebP, OptiPNG, and JPEGoptim. The late-command checksum-verifies pinned
   245	`pdfcpu` and Typst archives, installs them below `/usr/local/lib` with fixed
   246	`/usr/local/bin` links, and creates a root-owned Pipx environment under
   247	`/usr/local/lib/digital-assets/pipx` for `pdf2docx` and `pymupdf4llm`.
   248	The action wrapper uses that interpreter in isolated mode (`-I`) so it does
   249	not import user-site packages or honor Python environment overrides.
   250	Pandoc always uses Typst as its PDF engine, so this workflow does not require a
   251	LaTeX stack.
   252	
   253	PDF content editing creates a reflowable Markdown working copy, runs
   254	FocusWriter with native Wayland backends forced, and builds a new PDF with
   255	Pandoc plus Typst. It cannot preserve original page geometry, forms,
   256	signatures, annotations, or exact layout. PDF bookmark editing exports a
   257	private `bookmarks.json` working copy for Nano and imports it with pdfcpu into
   258	a new validated PDF. QDF hyperlink/typo edits use a bounded literal byte
   259	replacement followed by `fix-qdf` and QPDF validation; they invalidate
   260	signatures and do not preserve source encryption.
   261	
   262	Endpoint Security keeps selected
   263	file and folder operations
   264	unprivileged, while fixed host-wide audits and signature updates use the
   265	existing desktop-owned `10-pkexec.rules` policy and a root helper. System provides
   266	firmware, package, NVMe, Btrfs, journal, resolver, user-service, notification,
   267	Waybar, and external-drive maintenance alongside the existing host inspection
   268	actions. `Manage External Drives` inventories USB disks and volumes, reports
   269	mounted state, and delegates mount, sync-before-unmount, and confirmed
   270	sync/unmount/power-off operations to UDisks through the active desktop user's
   271	polkit session. The `usbmedia` policy names the actual UDisks2 actions used by
   272	GIO and Thunar, including `filesystem-unmount-others`; nonexistent
   273	`filesystem-unmount` and obsolete `drive-eject` action names are rejected by
   274	target verification so a denied unmount cannot tear down the browsing window
   275	without completing the requested operation. The Debian `eject` utility remains
   276	installed for Thunar/GIO compatibility, but the managed launcher does not
   277	bypass UDisks or force busy filesystems offline.
   278	Disruptive firmware, upgrade, journal, and audio actions require an explicit
